@@ -28,0 +29 @@ Requires the One Piece Mod (Fabric, Minecraft 26.3, Java 25).
+- **Shipwright's Forge and Grand Line Anvil:** tier 4 and 5 materials (Wapometal, Adam Wood, Kokuto, Dragon Scale, Netherite) have no crafting table part recipes. Stoke a Shipwright's Forge with coal, sulfur, blaze rods or lava, then hold any part as the pattern with the material in your offhand to forge a copy (one heat per piece of material). Gear with any tier 4+ part is put together, mended and upgraded only at a Grand Line Anvil (a Shipwright's Anvil braced with obsidian and a Netherite or Wapometal ingot); the Marine Armory Bench also works Navy tier 5 gear. Town blacksmiths won't touch these materials. See `station/HighTier`.
@@ -39 +40 @@ Requires the One Piece Mod (Fabric, Minecraft 26.3, Java 25).
-Pirate and shared materials' parts are made at a crafting table from 1 to 8 of a material (Navy materials' parts come from the captured Navy stations instead), each part in its own shape (the recipe book shows them all). Armor shells have a leather pad in the middle so they don't clash with vanilla armor. Model and recipe JSON is generated by `tools/gen_resources.py` (run it after changing `materials.json`).
+Pirate and shared materials' parts up to tier 3 are made at a crafting table from 1 to 8 of a material (tier 4+ at the Shipwright's Forge, and Navy materials' parts come from the captured Navy stations instead), each part in its own shape (the recipe book shows them all). Armor shells have a leather pad in the middle so they don't clash with vanilla armor. Model and recipe JSON is generated by `tools/gen_resources.py` (run it after changing `materials.json`).
